---
title: Chicken teriyaki
servings: 2
tags: [japanese, chicken, quick, weeknight]
cuisine: japanese
time: 20 minutes
source: Chicken Teriyaki by Namiko Hirasawa Chen, Just One Cookbook, https://www.justonecookbook.com/chicken-teriyaki/
---

== Sauce ==

Mix the @soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @mirin{2%tbsp}, @sake{2%tbsp} and @sugar{1%tbsp}
in a small bowl. Warm it in the microwave and stir until the sugar dissolves.

== Chicken ==

Lay the @chicken thighs{3/4-1%lb}(boneless, skin-on if you can find them)
smooth side down. Cut slits 1/2 inch apart without going all the way through,
deeper where the meat is thick, and press them open to an even thickness.
Season both sides lightly with @kosher salt{1/8%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/8%tsp}.

Heat a large #frying pan{} with a lid over medium to medium-high heat. Add the
@neutral oil{1%tbsp} and lay the chicken in smooth side down. Press it flat
with a #spatula{} for a few seconds and cook ~{5%minutes}.

Turn it, press again, then lower the heat, cover, and steam ~{3%minutes}.

Uncover and wipe out the fat with a paper towel.

Turn the heat to medium and pour in the sauce. Tilt the pan and spoon the sauce
over the chicken until it is glazed and cooked through. Move it to a board.

Let the sauce bubble until it is a little thinner than you want; it thickens as
it cools. Slice the chicken and serve with the sauce, over rice if you like.

> Optional: char the cut sides briefly under the broiler before serving.
